the google cloud sdk what is it  the google cloud software development  kit is a collection of tools that are  used to interact with google cloud apis  and services and manage the resources in  your google cloud projects  together these tools help developers and  technical practitioners be more  efficient when interacting with google  cloud  the sdk includes the google cloud cli  cloud client libraries  developer tools and documentation  the first piece of the google cloud sdk  is the google cloud cli a collection of  command line tools you can install to  access and manage your cloud from the  command line  with it you can do all kinds of things  like manage virtual machines query  bigquery tables  update cool cloud storage buckets and  virtually anything else you can do in  the cloud console all from your linux  mac os or windows terminal  next in our sdk are cloud client  libraries for programmatically  integrating google cloud apis into your  code  with high level api abstractions cloud  client libraries handle all the  low-level details of communicating with  google cloud  this greatly reduces the boilerplate  code you would have to write otherwise  and lowers a learning curve so you can  hit the ground running and start coding  effectively and more quickly most  importantly cloud client libraries are  available for several programming  languages including java python node.js  go ruby c-sharp and php each sdk will  also have language specific frameworks  and tools as available so you'll have  everything you need no matter what your  favorite language is  cloud client libraries are available for  more than 100 google cloud services to  help you better understand how to best  use them the google cloud sdk also  includes detailed documentation that  we've centralized on cloud.google.com  so you'll always have access to  consistent authoritative and update  technical reference documentation and  code snippets  and finally the sdk optionally includes  cloud code an ide extension available  for vs code and intellij that helps you  write debug and deploy cloud native apps  all without ever needing a switch from  your ide window  do you want to get started using the  google cloud sdk  the google cloud cli is available via  your operating system's package manager  or a direct download from  cloud.google.com and cloud client  libraries can be installed via standard  library package managers like npm and  pip or via the language-specific google  cloud client library's repositories  linked in the description of this video  to learn more about the google cloud sdk  check out cloud.google.com  sdk  [Music]  you
 

